   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# Claude_for_search\n\n**Parameter search for optimal opacity figure**  \n- Fix $\\\\rho = r = 0.9$, $\\\\gamma = 1.85$  \n- Search over $\\\\phi \\\\in [0.005, 0.1]$, $\\\\omega_u > 0$, $n \\\\geq 2$, $c_s > 0$  \n- Target conditions:  \n  - **(2a)** Three clear phases: A (jump to $\\\\omega_L$), B (jump to $\\\\omega_H$), C (flat $\\\\rightarrow$ increasing)  \n  - **(2b)** Phase A and B transitions at **sizable** $\\\\omega_s$ values (not negligibly small)  \n- Best candidate: $\\\\phi=0.030$, $n=5$, $\\\\omega_u=5.0$, $c_s=10^{-4}$ \u2192 $R = \\\\omega_{s2}/\\\\omega_{s1} \\\\approx 3.0$"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "b01c242e",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "\"\"\"\nSection A: Function Definitions\nSame structure as Claude_for_.ipynb; phi passed explicitly (no global).\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom itertools import product\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\ndef thetafunc(phi_v, we, n):\n    return (1 - phi_v) * (n - 1) / (n * phi_v)\n\ndef solve_G(we, wu, phi_v, n):\n    a = we / wu\n    theta = thetafunc(phi_v, we, n)\n    A = 2*a - 1 - 2*theta\n    B = a*a - 2*a\n    C = -a*a\n    roots = np.roots([1, A, B, C])\n    real_roots = sorted([float(r.real) for r in roots if np.isreal(r) and r.real > 1])\n    return real_roots\n\ndef U(z, wu, ws, we, cs, gamma, n, phi_v):\n    theta = thetafunc(phi_v, we, n)\n    return np.sqrt(ws) * phi_v * (1 + theta) * np.sqrt(z * wu) / (1 + z) - cs * (we ** gamma)\n\ndef theta_cutoff(we, wu):\n    if we == 0:\n        return np.nan, np.nan\n    h = wu / we\n    a_coeff = 8 * h**3\n    b_coeff = h * (8*h*h - 20*h - 1)\n    c_coeff = 2 * (1 + h)**3\n    t0 = 27 / (16 * h)\n    th, tl = t0, t0\n    if we > 8 * wu:\n        D = b_coeff**2 - 4 * a_coeff * c_coeff\n        if D >= 0:\n            tl = 0.5 * (-b_coeff - np.sqrt(D)) / a_coeff\n            th = 0.5 * (-b_coeff + np.sqrt(D)) / a_coeff\n    return th, tl\n\ndef we_cutoff_auto(phi_v, wu, n):\n    \"\"\"Dynamically find omega_L (cross_th) and omega_H (cross_tl).\"\"\"\n    we_grid = np.linspace(0.001, 100 * wu, 4000)\n    theta_val = thetafunc(phi_v, 1, n)\n    th_line = np.array([theta_cutoff(we, wu)[0] for we in we_grid])\n    tl_line = np.array([theta_cutoff(we, wu)[1] for we in we_grid])\n    cross_th = cross_tl = None\n    for i in range(len(we_grid) - 1):\n        d0, d1 = theta_val - th_line[i], theta_val - th_line[i+1]\n        if not (np.isnan(d0) or np.isnan(d1)) and d0 * d1 < 0:\n            cross_th = we_grid[i] - d0 * (we_grid[i+1]-we_grid[i]) / (d1-d0)\n            break\n    for i in range(len(we_grid) - 1):\n        d0, d1 = theta_val - tl_line[i], theta_val - tl_line[i+1]\n        if not (np.isnan(d0) or np.isnan(d1)) and d0 * d1 < 0:\n            cross_tl = we_grid[i] - d0 * (we_grid[i+1]-we_grid[i]) / (d1-d0)\n            break\n    if cross_th is None or cross_tl is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No crossing found\")\n    return cross_th, cross_tl   # omega_L, omega_H\n\ndef result(cs, wu, phi_v, ws_grid, r, we_grid, gamma, n):\n    z_min = np.full(len(we_grid), np.nan)\n    z_max = np.full(len(we_grid), np.nan)\n    for i, we_val in enumerate(we_grid):\n        roots = solve_G(we_val, wu, phi_v, n)\n        if roots:\n            z_min[i] = roots[0]\n            z_max[i] = roots[-1]\n    we_star = np.full(len(ws_grid), np.nan)\n    for j, ws_val in enumerate(ws_grid):\n        u_min = U(z_min, wu, ws_val, we_grid, cs, gamma, n, phi_v)\n        u_max = U(z_max, wu, ws_val, we_grid, cs, gamma, n, phi_v)\n        u_av = r * u_min + (1 - r) * u_max\n        if not np.all(np.isnan(u_av)):\n            we_star[j] = we_grid[np.nanargmax(u_av)]\n    return we_star, ws_grid\n\ndef find_jumps(we_star, ws_grid, threshold):\n    diffs = np.abs(np.diff(we_star))\n    jumps = []\n    for i in np.where(diffs > threshold)[0]:\n        if not jumps or ws_grid[i] - jumps[-1] > (ws_grid[-1]-ws_grid[0])*0.01:\n            jumps.append(float(ws_grid[i]))\n    return jumps\n\ndef draw_broken_axis(ax_top, ax_bot, x, y, y_lim, r_val, loc):\n    threshold = (y_lim[3] - y_lim[0]) * 0.1\n    jump_indices = np.where(np.abs(np.diff(y)) > threshold)[0]\n    x_split = np.insert(x.astype(float), jump_indices + 1, np.nan)\n    y_split = np.insert(y.astype(float), jump_indices + 1, np.nan)\n    for ax in [ax_top, ax_bot]:\n        ax.plot(x_split, y_split, 'b-', lw=2., zorder=2, label=f'$\\\\rho = {r_val}$')\n        for idx in jump_indices:\n            ax.plot(x[idx],   y[idx],   'bo', markersize=6, zorder=3)\n            ax.plot(x[idx+1], y[idx+1], 'bo', markersize=6, zorder=3)\n            ax.vlines(x[idx], y[idx], y[idx+1], colors='blue', linestyles='dotted', lw=1)\n    ax_bot.set_ylim(y_lim[0], y_lim[1])\n    ax_top.set_ylim(y_lim[2], y_lim[3])\n    ax_top.spines['bottom'].set_visible(False)\n    ax_bot.spines['top'].set_visible(False)\n    ax_top.tick_params(labelbottom=False, bottom=False)\n    ax_top.spines['right'].set_visible(False)\n    ax_top.spines['top'].set_visible(False)\n    ax_bot.spines['right'].set_visible(False)\n    fig = plt.gcf()\n    d = 0.005\n    for ax in [ax_top, ax_bot]:\n        pos = ax.transAxes.transform([0, 0 if ax == ax_top else 1])\n        pf  = fig.transFigure.inverted().transform(pos)\n        fig.lines.append(plt.Line2D(\n            (pf[0]-d, pf[0]+d), (pf[1]-d, pf[1]+d),\n            transform=fig.transFigure, color='k', lw=1))\n    handles, labels = ax_top.get_legend_handles_labels()\n    ax_top.legend(dict(zip(labels, handles)).values(),\n                  dict(zip(labels, handles)).keys(),\n                  loc=loc, fontsize=12, frameon=False)\n\nprint(\"Functions defined.\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c8fab8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Section B: Parameter Search\n\nSearch over $\\\\phi$, $n$, $\\\\omega_u$ with $r = \\\\rho = 0.9$ fixed.  \nFor each candidate, detect jump locations $\\\\omega_{s1}$ (Phase A\u2192B) and $\\\\omega_{s2}$ (Phase B\u2192C),  \nand compute $R = \\\\omega_{s2}/\\\\omega_{s1}$ (smaller = more balanced phases).  \nKeep only candidates where Phase C (above $\\\\omega_H$) also exists."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "0eeb2582",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# ============================================================\n# Section B: Parameter Search  (r = rho = 0.9 fixed)\n# ============================================================\nr      = 0.9      # <<< FIXED (rho)\ngamma  = 1.85\n\nphi_vals = [0.010, 0.015, 0.020, 0.025, 0.030, 0.050]\nn_vals   = [3, 5, 8, 10, 20]\nwu_vals  = [1.0, 3.3, 5.0, 10.0]\ncs_probe = 1e-4\n\nresults_search = []\nfor phi_v, n_v, wu_v in product(phi_vals, n_vals, wu_vals):\n    try:\n        wL, wH = we_cutoff_auto(phi_v, wu_v, n_v)\n    except:\n        continue\n    we_g = np.linspace(0, wH * 1.6, 1500)\n    theta_v  = thetafunc(phi_v, 1, n_v)\n    gain_est = phi_v * (1 + theta_v) * np.sqrt(wu_v) * 0.3\n    ws1_est  = (cs_probe * wL**gamma / max(gain_est, 1e-12))**2\n    ws_max_p = max(3.0, ws1_est * 200)\n    ws_probe = np.linspace(0, ws_max_p, 1500)\n    try:\n        we_p, _ = result(cs_probe, wu_v, phi_v, ws_probe, r, we_g, gamma, n_v)\n    except:\n        continue\n    if np.all(np.isnan(we_p)):\n        continue\n    jumps = find_jumps(we_p, ws_probe, wL * 0.07)\n    if len(jumps) < 2:\n        continue\n    ws1, ws2 = jumps[0], jumps[1]\n    R = ws2 / ws1 if ws1 > 1e-9 else np.inf\n    if not np.isfinite(R):\n        continue\n    if np.nanmax(we_p) < wH * 0.95:\n        continue  # Phase C must exist\n    results_search.append(dict(phi=phi_v, n=n_v, wu=wu_v, theta=theta_v,\n                                wL=wL, wH=wH, ws1=ws1, ws2=ws2, R=R))\n\nresults_search.sort(key=lambda x: x['R'])\nprint(f\"{'phi':>6} {'n':>4} {'wu':>5} {'theta':>7} {'wL':>7} {'wH':>7}  {'ws1':>8} {'ws2':>8}   R\")\nprint(\"-\"*72)\nfor rec in results_search[:15]:\n    print(f\"{rec['phi']:>6.3f} {rec['n']:>4} {rec['wu']:>5.1f} {rec['theta']:>7.1f} \"\n          f\"{rec['wL']:>7.2f} {rec['wH']:>7.2f}  {rec['ws1']:>8.4f} {rec['ws2']:>8.4f}  {rec['R']:>5.2f}\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a23e671b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Section C: Final Parameters and Computation\n\nBest candidate: **$\\\\phi=0.030$, $n=5$, $\\\\omega_u=5.0$, $c_s=10^{-4}$**  \n- $R \\\\approx 3.0$ (vs. $R \\\\approx 17$+ in original parameters)  \n- $\\\\omega_{s1} \\\\approx 0.14$, $\\\\omega_{s2} \\\\approx 0.41$ (30\u201350\u00d7 more visible than original)  \n- $\\\\theta \\\\approx 25.9$, $\\\\omega_L \\\\approx 60.9$, $\\\\omega_H \\\\approx 70.1$"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "3b66f728",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# ============================================================\n# Section C: Final Parameters \u2192 Computation\n# ============================================================\nphi_f  = 0.030\nn_f    = 5\nwu_f   = 5.0\ncs_f   = 1e-4\nr      = 0.9\ngamma  = 1.85\n\nwL_f, wH_f = we_cutoff_auto(phi_f, wu_f, n_f)\nprint(f\"phi={phi_f}, n={n_f}, wu={wu_f}, cs={cs_f}, r={r}\")\nprint(f\"omega_L = {wL_f:.3f}   omega_H = {wH_f:.3f}\")\nprint(f\"theta   = {thetafunc(phi_f, 1, n_f):.2f}\")\n\nwe_grid_f = np.linspace(0, wH_f * 2.0, 8000)\n\n# First pass: locate ws1, ws2 precisely on a wide grid\nws_wide   = np.linspace(0.0, 0.8, 8000)\nwe_wide, _= result(cs_f, wu_f, phi_f, ws_wide, r, we_grid_f, gamma, n_f)\njumps_wide= find_jumps(we_wide, ws_wide, wL_f * 0.08)\nws1_f, ws2_f = jumps_wide[0], jumps_wide[1]\nprint(f\"\\nJump A (ws1) = {ws1_f:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Jump B (ws2) = {ws2_f:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"R            = {ws2_f/ws1_f:.2f}\")\n\n# Panel A: ws from 0 to just past jump A  \u2192  shows Phase A\u2192B transition\nws_grid_a = np.linspace(0.000, ws1_f * 1.35, 5000)\nwe_star_a, _ = result(cs_f, wu_f, phi_f, ws_grid_a, r, we_grid_f, gamma, n_f)\n\n# Panel B: ws from just above jump A to past jump B  \u2192  shows Phase B\u2192C transition\nws_grid_b = np.linspace(ws1_f * 1.02, ws2_f * 1.35, 5000)\nwe_star_b, _ = result(cs_f, wu_f, phi_f, ws_grid_b, r, we_grid_f, gamma, n_f)\n\n# Panel C: ws from just above jump B onward  \u2192  shows flat Phase C then rising\nws_grid_c = np.linspace(ws2_f * 1.02, ws2_f * 200.0, 5000)\nwe_star_c, _ = result(cs_f, wu_f, phi_f, ws_grid_c, r, we_grid_f, gamma, n_f)\n\nprint(f\"Phase C max we* = {np.nanmax(we_star_c):.2f}\")\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c1d7c29b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Section D: Plot\n\nThree-panel broken-axis figure showing optimal opacity $\\\\omega_{\eta}^*$ vs. average skill $\\\\omega_s$.  \nEach panel focuses on one phase transition."
  },
